abstract: |
  Aurora-GLM is a modular, extensible, and high-performance Python framework for
  generalized linear models (GLM), generalized additive models (GAM), and generalized
  additive mixed models (GAMM). It supports multiple distribution families, link functions,
  smooth terms, random effects, and temporal covariance structures, with multi-backend
  support for NumPy, PyTorch, and JAX.
